@inproceedings{dasgupta_pitfalls_2024,
 abstract = {This article proposes a compact and efficient all-solid-state Marx generator with a novel triggering scheme for driving a repetitive pulsed power system. The generator consists of 10 stages, each stage including a primary capacitor, a spark gap switch, and a pulse forming network (PFN). The PFN is composed of two capacitors and two inductors, which can sharpen the pulse and increase the output voltage. The triggering scheme uses a single trigger pulse to sequentially trigger all spark gap switches, which simplifies the control system and improves the reliability. A prototype of the Marx generator is built and tested. Experimental results show that the generator can produce a 10 kV output voltage with a 100 ns rise time and a 200 ns pulse width at a repetition rate of 100 Hz. The generator has a compact size of 200 mm × 150 mm × 100 mm and a total weight of 5 kg, which is suitable for portable applications.},
