 abstract = {We present GarmentStudio, a framework for high-fidelity neural 3D reconstruction of clothed humans from multi-view images. Existing methods either struggle with loose garments or require garment templates. We propose a novel pipeline that disentangles body and garment representations, enabling realistic reconstruction of diverse garment types, including loose and multi-layered clothing. Our approach leverages a layered neural representation with a body-conditioned garment model, trained on a large-scale synthetic dataset. We introduce a self-supervised training strategy that aligns multi-view images with the reconstructed geometry, ensuring photorealistic results. Extensive experiments demonstrate that GarmentStudio outperforms state-of-the-art methods in reconstruction quality and generalization to unseen garments and poses.},
