 abstract = {This paper proposes a novel framework for the detection and classification of anomalies in multivariate time series data, specifically tailored for industrial applications in the context of Industry 4.0. The approach integrates deep learning techniques, including autoencoders and recurrent neural networks, to capture temporal dependencies and spatial correlations within the data. The framework is evaluated on real-world datasets from manufacturing processes, demonstrating superior performance in terms of accuracy, precision, and recall compared to traditional statistical methods and other machine learning baselines. The results highlight the potential of the proposed method for real-time anomaly detection, enabling proactive maintenance and reducing downtime in smart factories.},
