 abstract = {This chapter presents a novel framework for enhancing the security of blockchain-based supply chain management systems through the integration of zero-knowledge proofs (ZKPs) and multi-party computation (MPC). We address key challenges such as data privacy, traceability, and tamper-resistance in decentralized environments. Our approach leverages zk-SNARKs to enable verifiable computations without revealing sensitive information, while MPC ensures collaborative decision-making among untrusted parties. Experimental evaluations on a simulated supply chain network demonstrate significant improvements in transaction throughput (up to 40%) and privacy preservation, with minimal overhead in proof generation time. The proposed system is particularly suited for industries requiring high confidentiality, such as pharmaceuticals and luxury goods.},
