 abstract = {Visual Question Answering (VQA) has achieved remarkable progress with the development of large vision-language models. However, the fairness issue in VQA has been overlooked, which may lead to biased predictions for certain groups. In this paper, we conduct a comprehensive study on fairness in VQA from three perspectives: data, model, and evaluation. We first analyze the bias in existing VQA datasets and propose a new dataset, FairVQA, to mitigate the bias. Then, we investigate the fairness of state-of-the-art VQA models and find that they exhibit significant bias. Finally, we propose a fairness evaluation metric and benchmark for VQA. Our work provides insights into fair VQA and paves the way for future research.},
