 abstract = {This paper introduces VisFlow, a novel visual analytics system designed to facilitate the exploration and analysis of dynamic graph data in cybersecurity applications. By integrating temporal graph visualization with interactive flow analysis, VisFlow enables users to detect anomalous patterns and track evolving threats in network traffic. Our system employs a hybrid layout algorithm that combines force-directed placement with time-based slicing to maintain readability across large-scale datasets. We demonstrate the effectiveness of VisFlow through case studies on real-world intrusion detection datasets, highlighting its advantages in identifying stealthy attacks that traditional methods overlook. The results show improved detection accuracy and reduced analysis time compared to baseline tools.},
