 abstract = {Federated learning (FL) enables collaborative model training across distributed devices while preserving data privacy. However, integrating large language models (LLMs) into FL introduces significant challenges, including substantial communication overhead, intensive computational requirements, and heightened privacy risks due to the models' scale and complexity. In this paper, we propose SecureFedLLM, a novel framework that addresses these issues through a combination of efficient parameter selection, secure multi-party computation, and adaptive aggregation techniques. Our approach reduces communication costs by up to 70% and enhances privacy guarantees against inference attacks, as demonstrated on benchmark datasets with popular LLMs like GPT-3 and LLaMA. Experimental results show that SecureFedLLM maintains comparable accuracy to centralized training while outperforming existing FL methods for LLMs in terms of efficiency and security.},
