@article{noauthor_ecr_2025,
 abstract = {Background Artificial intelligence (AI) is revolutionizing radiology by enhancing diagnostic accuracy, improving workflow efficiency, and enabling personalized patient care. This review explores the current applications of AI in radiology and discusses future directions. Main body We examine AI applications across various imaging modalities, including computer-aided detection and diagnosis (CAD) systems for chest radiography, mammography, and CT. AI also facilitates image segmentation, quantification, and predictive analytics for disease prognosis. Key challenges include data quality, algorithmic bias, regulatory hurdles, and ethical considerations such as transparency and accountability. Future prospects encompass explainable AI, federated learning for privacy-preserving models, and integration with other technologies like augmented reality. Conclusion AI has the potential to transform radiology practice, but successful adoption requires interdisciplinary collaboration, robust validation, and adherence to ethical standards to ensure equitable and safe implementation.},
