 abstract = {Federated learning (FL) has emerged as a promising paradigm for collaborative machine learning without the need to centralize sensitive data. However, deploying FL in real-world scenarios, especially over wireless networks, introduces unique challenges due to the heterogeneity of devices, limited communication resources, and privacy concerns. This paper provides a comprehensive survey on FL over wireless networks, focusing on the key challenges and recent advances. We first introduce the fundamentals of FL and its integration with wireless communications. Then, we discuss the main challenges in wireless FL, including communication efficiency, resource allocation, incentive mechanisms, and security & privacy. For each challenge, we review the state-of-the-art solutions and highlight open research issues. Finally, we outline future research directions to advance the deployment of FL in wireless environments.},
