@incollection{sekrst_hallucinations_2025,
 abstract = {This chapter proposes a novel framework for enhancing the security and privacy of federated learning systems using blockchain technology. Federated learning allows multiple devices to collaboratively train a shared model without exchanging raw data, addressing privacy concerns in traditional machine learning. However, it faces challenges such as single points of failure, malicious participants, and lack of transparency. By integrating blockchain, we ensure decentralized model aggregation, tamper-proof audit trails, and incentive mechanisms for honest participation. Our approach employs smart contracts for automated validation and consensus on model updates. Experimental results on benchmark datasets demonstrate improved robustness against poisoning attacks and Byzantine faults, with minimal overhead in communication and computation. This work paves the way for secure, scalable federated learning in real-world applications like healthcare and IoT.},
