 abstract = {Diabetic Retinopathy (DR) is one of the major causes of blindness in the world. Early detection and treatment can prevent vision loss. In this paper, we propose a deep learning-based approach for the detection of DR using fundus images. The proposed model uses a convolutional neural network (CNN) architecture to classify fundus images into five stages: No DR, Mild, Moderate, Severe, and Proliferative DR. The model is trained on the APTOS 2019 Blindness Detection dataset, which contains 3,662 training images and 1,928 testing images. The proposed model achieves an accuracy of 92.5%, precision of 93.1%, recall of 92.5%, and F1-score of 92.8% on the test set. The results show that the proposed model outperforms state-of-the-art methods in terms of accuracy and computational efficiency. The proposed approach can be used for automated screening of DR in resource-limited settings.},
