 abstract = {Interactive data visualization tools have become essential for exploring complex datasets, but creating effective visualizations often requires significant expertise in both data analysis and visual design. To address this, we introduce VizML, a machine learning-based system that automatically generates visualization recommendations for a given dataset. VizML uses a combination of statistical analysis and deep learning to suggest chart types, encodings, and layouts that best convey the underlying patterns in the data. We evaluate VizML through a user study with 30 participants, comparing it to manual visualization creation and existing automated tools. Results show that VizML significantly reduces creation time while producing visualizations rated as equally effective and aesthetically pleasing. Our findings highlight the potential of ML-assisted tools to democratize data visualization.},
