 abstract = {Multimodal data fusion is a critical task in many real-world applications, where information from multiple modalities (e.g., text, image, audio) needs to be integrated to make informed decisions. Deep learning has shown great success in handling unimodal data, but fusing multimodal data presents unique challenges due to heterogeneity, alignment, and missing data issues. This chapter provides a comprehensive survey of deep learning-based methods for multimodal data fusion. We categorize the existing approaches into early fusion, late fusion, and hybrid fusion strategies, and discuss their architectures, advantages, and limitations. Furthermore, we highlight key applications in areas such as healthcare, autonomous driving, and sentiment analysis. Finally, we identify open challenges and future research directions to advance the field.},
