 abstract = {Federated learning (FL) enables collaborative model training across distributed devices while preserving data privacy by keeping raw data local. However, deploying FL in the Internet of Things (IoT) environments poses unique challenges due to resource constraints, heterogeneity, and security vulnerabilities. This survey provides a comprehensive overview of FL for resource-constrained IoT devices, categorizing existing approaches into communication-efficient, computation-efficient, and privacy-preserving techniques. We discuss key enablers such as model compression, edge computing integration, and secure aggregation protocols. Furthermore, we analyze open challenges including non-IID data distribution, incentive mechanisms, and scalability in large-scale IoT networks. Finally, we outline future research directions, emphasizing the role of FL in enabling intelligent, privacy-aware IoT ecosystems for 6G and beyond.},
